	(text "The Odyssey 2 / Videopac cartridge port (Dan Boris, O2 Tech Specs 2.0): 1-15 on the parts face, A-R behind them.\nA0-A11 latched, DB0-DB7 the 8048 bus, /PSEN reads the cart, /WR writes (off while P16 is high), P10 / P11 the\nbank lines, P14 the write select, E the external-RAM enable, T0 the 8048 test input (cart -> console).\nEvery line reaches the RP2354B through 330R, in the PicoPAC map (picopac_cart.c): GPIO0-11 A0-A11, 12 P11,\n13 P10, 14-21 DB0-DB7, 22 /PSEN, 23 /WR, 24 P14, 26 E, 27 T0.  GPIO0-39 are 5 V tolerant while IOVDD is up.\nB: GND on a G7000; on a Videopac+ low shows the 8245 everywhere -- 10k down, 1k from GP28 to raise it.\nGP40 senses the console 5 V (10k / 15k = 3.0 V); GP25 drives the LED; GP29 / GP44 / GP45 are bring-up pads."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 132.08 40.64 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "4d44fe1d-09a8-5dfb-ad6d-8a5a76bcab50")
	)
